2026-08-01 17:02:52,253 INFO Chat response:
Sure! There are three recommendations, all aimed at KidsFlix's low mobile money conversion in the DRC:

First, since PAYMENT_NOT_APPROVED and OTHER_ERROR are the biggest failure reasons, it's worth checking whether the checkout flow makes it clear enough to users that they need to complete the operator-side approval step (entering a PIN or confirming via USSD) before the payment times out - a confusing or rushed prompt could be causing otherwise-willing customers to fail approval.

Second, for users hitting "Too many requests" or "Subscription limit exceeded" errors, adding clearer messaging or a short cooldown period would help them understand why their payment was blocked, rather than just seeing a failure and possibly giving up or retrying incorrectly.

Third, since insufficient balance accounts for a meaningful chunk of failures, a lightweight nudge to check their balance before starting the payment could help users avoid initiating a payment they can't complete, reducing abandoned attempts.

Happy to go deeper on any one of these if you'd like.
