Of course! There are three recommendations in the summary, all aimed at KidsFlix's DRC mobile money performance. First, since PAYMENT_NOT_APPROVED is by far the biggest failure reason (4,370 occurrences), the suggestion is to dig into why customers aren't approving the mobile money prompt and to improve in-app messaging or add retry prompts to help them complete it. Second, because insufficient balance and rate-limit/subscription-limit errors (like "Too many requests" and "Subscription limit exceeded") also make up a meaningful chunk of failures, using softer, delayed retry logic instead of immediately resubmitting could cut down on those rejections. Third, since Airtel handles the largest volume of attempts (4,427) but isn't converting proportionally better than the smaller Orange or Vodacom M-Pesa channels, reviewing Airtel-specific prompt timing or UX is recommended, since even a small improvement there would have the biggest overall impact given its volume. Happy to go deeper on any one of these three if you'd like.
