{"services": [{"product_id": 5321, "summary": "VUZ360's payment performance in Uganda was weak across both days of this period, with conversion staying low and fairly consistent day to day rather than one day dragging down an otherwise healthy trend. The dominant driver is customer-side insufficient balance, which together accounts for the large majority of failures, followed by a sizable share of unknown-reason failures and a meaningful chunk of authorization timeouts at the mobile network operator level. Both MTN and Airtel show similarly poor conversion, with MTN carrying the bulk of attempts, indicating this is a broad market-condition issue rather than one operator being uniquely at fault. Volume was concentrated in a few peak hours each day (notably mid-afternoon on the 24th and evening on the 25th), but those high-traffic windows did not convert any better than the quieter hours.", "recommendations": ["Since insufficient funds and MNO authorization timeouts dominate failures on both MTN and Airtel, consider adding retry prompts or delayed-retry logic so customers can attempt payment again once they've topped up, rather than losing the transaction outright.", "Investigate the unknown-reason failure bucket with pawapay, as it represents a large enough share of failures to be worth root-causing separately from the funds-related issues.", "Given the concentrated peak-hour volume (afternoon on the 24th, evening on the 25th) showing no conversion improvement over quieter periods, this doesn't appear to be a load/capacity issue, so focus remediation on payment-method education or balance-check prompts before checkout instead."], "notable_days": [], "notable_hours": []}]}
