{"services": [{"product_id": 5345, "summary": "Learn2bFit150's transactions in India are overwhelmingly routed through UPI, which carries nearly all volume but converts at a low rate, dragging the overall picture down. The dominant failure reason by far is request timing out, well ahead of insufficient funds and outright payment declines, pointing to UPI collect requests going unacknowledged rather than users actively rejecting payments. Across the week performance is fairly choppy day to day, with Sunday standing out as a clear low point even though it carried by far the heaviest volume of the period, while the lighter-volume Wednesday posted the strongest conversion. Within days, the pattern is also uneven by hour: late evening hours tend to carry the bulk of attempts, and on Sunday the two hours spanning 8pm-10pm saw a huge surge in volume that converted poorly, pulling that whole day down.", "recommendations": ["Investigate UPI collect-request timeouts specifically around the high-volume evening window (8-10pm), since that's where most failed volume is concentrated.", "Consider shortening the UPI payment request expiry or adding a retry/reminder nudge before timeout, since timeouts outnumber every other failure reason combined.", "Treat emandate as effectively non-functional for this flow given its near-total failure rate on the small sample it got, and review whether it should be offered as a payment option at all."], "notable_days": ["2026-10-05"], "notable_hours": ["2026-10-05T20:00:00", "2026-10-05T21:00:00"]}]}
