{"services": [{"product_id": 5290, "summary": "KidsFlix Monthly's Zambian mobile money traffic converted at a low rate over this two-day window, driven overwhelmingly by customers not approving the payment in time (or mistyping their PIN) and, secondarily, insufficient funds at the moment of charge - both market-side frictions rather than anything on the integration itself. Across operators, Zamtel converted essentially nobody while carrying meaningful volume, MTN also lagged well behind Airtel, which handled the bulk of attempts and converted noticeably better. The two days were fairly close in rate, though October 12 carried the vast majority of volume while October 13's traffic tapered off sharply after mid-morning with no further activity recorded for the rest of that day. Within October 12, performance held up reasonably steadily through the day with scattered weak pockets overnight and in the early morning hours. On the placement side, a handful of individual app placements (health tracker, downloader, and chat-bot style apps) converted noticeably worse than the broader mix despite real volume, while device-level results were fairly consistent aside from Xiaomi lagging slightly.", "recommendations": ["Investigate why Zamtel transactions are converting at essentially zero despite real volume - this points to a network-side routing or eligibility issue worth raising with pawapay rather than something fixable in-app.", "Consider deprioritizing or excluding the weaker-converting app placements (e.g. com.vita.track.health, com.fbvideodownloader.downloadfbvideos, com.merryblue.facebookvideodownloader) from campaign targeting, since they bring volume but rarely convert.", "Since PIN non-approval and insufficient funds dominate failures, consider adjusting retry/reminder messaging timing for customers rather than changing the payment flow itself, as these are customer-side behaviors outside DTPay's or KidsFlix's control."], "notable_days": [], "notable_hours": [], "campaign_overview": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 and the Zambia Hybrid Minime campaign converted modestly better than Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1, consistent with the latter routing a larger share of its volume through MTN, which underperforms Airtel across the board; Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2's volume is too low to draw a real conclusion from. Reasons are broadly similar across campaigns, with PIN non-approval and insufficient funds dominating everywhere.", "campaigns": [{"campaign_id": "HbDnGOiytpqHfNwTO6AD", "summary": "Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1 converted somewhat below the service average, likely tied to its heavier reliance on MTN relative to Airtel, alongside the same PIN-approval and balance issues seen elsewhere."}, {"campaign_id": "UvPMMgS5CLykqt3xhBkV", "summary": "Zambia Hybrid Minime-kidsflix converted close to the service average, routing most of its volume through the better-performing Airtel network, though a few individual app placements (notably the health tracker and Facebook video downloader apps) dragged on an otherwise stronger mix."}, {"campaign_id": "fkfYl9lNcTJFSP6u5VZR", "summary": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 was the best-converting of the higher-volume campaigns, again correlating with a heavier skew toward Airtel over MTN."}, {"campaign_id": "BsLy4VuoZv6SsYu4iPX5", "summary": "Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2's volume is too low to draw a real conclusion from."}]}]}
