2026-10-13 11:16:00,975 INFO Claude response for cp_id=122:
{"services": [{"product_id": 5290, "summary": "KidsFlix Monthly's Zambian mobile-money traffic converted at a low rate over the two days, with the overwhelming majority of failures driven by customers not approving the PIN prompt in time and by insufficient funds, together accounting for the vast bulk of all failed attempts. Airtel carried most of the volume but converted noticeably better than MTN, while Zamtel processed a smaller volume with zero successful payments, suggesting a flow issue specific to that network over this window. Volume was heavily concentrated on the first day, which also pulled the blended rate down slightly; the second day saw much lower volume (traffic effectively stopped after mid-morning) and a modestly better rate, though that's based on a thinner sample. Within the first day, conversion dipped hardest in the early morning hours and recovered somewhat through the afternoon and evening, though it stayed choppy hour to hour rather than following a clean pattern.", "recommendations": ["Zamtel is converting at essentially zero despite real attempt volume - treat this as a network-side issue outside your control, but consider deprioritizing Zamtel-originated traffic in your own campaign targeting if this persists.", "MTN is converting well below Airtel on comparable volume; if you can see which campaigns or placements skew toward MTN users, consider whether that mix is worth continued investment.", "The PIN-approval and insufficient-funds reasons dominate failures and are customer/network-side (timing out or lacking funds) - not fixable on your end, but worth messaging users to have funds ready and respond promptly to the PIN prompt."], "notable_days": [], "notable_hours": [], "campaign_overview": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 and the Zambia Hybrid Minime campaign converted modestly better than Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1, largely tracking each campaign's mix of Airtel versus MTN attempts rather than any difference in failure reasons, which look similar across all three main campaigns. Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2 ran on too little volume to draw a real conclusion from.", "campaigns": [{"campaign_id": "HbDnGOiytpqHfNwTO6AD", "summary": "Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1 posted the weakest conversion of the larger campaigns, consistent with it carrying a heavier share of MTN attempts (which underperformed Airtel) alongside the same dominant PIN-approval and insufficient-funds failure pattern."}, {"campaign_id": "UvPMMgS5CLykqt3xhBkV", "summary": "The Zambia Hybrid Minime campaign converted slightly above the service average, running almost entirely through Airtel, though the website placement static.phxfeeds.com brought meaningful volume with no completions at all and is worth excluding."}, {"campaign_id": "fkfYl9lNcTJFSP6u5VZR", "summary": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 had the best conversion of the main campaigns, again skewing toward Airtel over MTN, with the same PIN-approval and insufficient-funds reasons leading failures."}, {"campaign_id": "BsLy4VuoZv6SsYu4iPX5", "summary": "Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2's volume is too low to draw a real conclusion from, though it's worth noting none of its tracked mobile-app placements converted at all."}]}]}
