{"services": [{"product_id": 5290, "summary": "KidsFlix Monthly in Zambia converted at a low rate over the period, with the vast majority of failures coming from customers not approving the payment in time (or with the wrong PIN) and a large secondary chunk from insufficient funds - both market-side frictions rather than anything on the integration itself. Airtel carried the bulk of volume and produced most of the completions, while MTN converted far worse despite meaningful volume, and Zamtel failed outright across all of its attempts. Traffic was heavily concentrated on October 12, which ran slightly behind the shorter October 13; within October 12 the overnight and early-morning hours were thin and choppy, with one early-morning hour showing a brief, low-volume spike in conversion that isn't meaningful on its own. October 13 cuts off abruptly after mid-morning, reflecting a partial day of data rather than a real drop in demand.", "recommendations": ["Investigate why Zamtel is converting at essentially zero - this looks like a channel worth pausing or deprioritizing until correspondent-side issues are resolved.", "MTN is converting well below Airtel despite comparable attempt volume in places; consider whether MTN customers are being routed into a weaker authorization flow or face longer PIN-entry windows.", "Within tracked placements, apps like com.vita.track.health, com.fbvideodownloader.downloadfbvideos, com.merryblue.facebookvideodownloader and whatsap.stuar.sittus bring real volume but convert far below the mobile-app average - worth excluding or deprioritizing these in campaign targeting."], "notable_days": [], "notable_hours": [], "campaign_overview": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 and the Zambia Hybrid Minime campaign converted modestly better than Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1, though all three sit in a similar range and share the same underlying mix of unapproved payments and insufficient funds; Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2's volume is too low to read as a real signal. Differences across the larger campaigns track mostly with how much of their traffic leaned on Airtel versus MTN, since Airtel consistently outperformed MTN wherever both appeared.", "campaigns": [{"campaign_id": "HbDnGOiytpqHfNwTO6AD", "summary": "Wallet-OD-V2-ZMB-KF-1 posted the weakest conversion of the larger campaigns, consistent with it carrying the heaviest MTN exposure relative to Airtel among the group, alongside the same customer-approval and insufficient-funds pattern seen service-wide."}, {"campaign_id": "UvPMMgS5CLykqt3xhBkV", "summary": "The Zambia Hybrid Minime campaign converted slightly better than average, helped by being almost entirely routed through the stronger-performing Airtel channel rather than MTN."}, {"campaign_id": "fkfYl9lNcTJFSP6u5VZR", "summary": "Wallet-Mobi-V2-ZMB-KF-1 had the best conversion among the larger campaigns, again tracking with a heavier skew toward Airtel over MTN, though it still faces the same approval and balance-driven failures as the rest."}, {"campaign_id": "BsLy4VuoZv6SsYu4iPX5", "summary": "Wallet-JD-V2-ZMB-KF-2's volume is too low to draw a real conclusion from, despite showing the same failure reasons as the larger campaigns."}]}]}
